# Tome of the Dead 3E floor-item class glyphs + revealed trap plate (game.md §8.11 Q1, §1.5).
# DRAFT 2026-10-20 for user review (preview: assets/gfx/tiles/items3e.svg.html,
# tools/items_glyph_preview.py). Format = tools/tiles_convert.py / gfx_convert.py --mode tile:
# 8x8, '#' ink, '.' paper, MSB-left, 1 ink on BLACK paper (standing row = air row, attr paper 0,
# so no clash with any depth's ATTR_FLOOR: the floor is the next cell row down).
# Art sits low: row 7 = the resting edge on the floor line. Non-solid, flags 0.
# Class = glyph SHAPE; exact type = per-cell INK set when stamped (item-type table). The header
# attr below is the DEFAULT (first type of the class); variants listed per block.
# Not wired: ids/attrs go live in the staff 3E task after approval (tiles_common / tilesets).
#
# id 60 FLASK reuses the old T_POTION glyph (sprites/grid/item_potion.grid): no block here.

# --- id 61 FOOD: tilted drumstick, meat top-left (paper shine), bone + knob down-right.
#     ink: meat $42 (default), cheese $46, pear $04, apple $44, carrot $06.
=== food ink:red paper:black bright
..###...
.#####..
##.####.
#.#####.
######..
.#####..
....##.#
.....##.

